-- INDEPENDENT tests of the Encouragement of Aliyah and Return (Temporary Provision) Law, 5786-2026.
-- Author: fid-il-36, run id IL-56-36-20261008.  Every expected value below is one decided in
-- DECIDED-ANSWERS.md (frozen, sha256 recorded in INDEPENDENT-FINDINGS.md) BEFORE the encoding was opened.
-- The id in each heading is that file's case id.  Nothing here was changed to match the encoding.
--
-- Where the default of the encoding refuses (a fork whose readings differ) and DECIDED-ANSWERS.md flagged the
-- same ambiguity, the assertion is #ASSERT REFUSED at the default and the reading I took is asserted by name.
-- Where DECIDED-ANSWERS.md decided a reading without flagging it, only the named reading is asserted.
-- Money is new shekels; a day is YMD year month day.

§ `Independent tests`

§§ `Shorthand`

GIVEN `the readings` IS A `The readings`
      `the person`   IS AN `An individual`
      `the items`    IS A LIST OF `An item of income`
      `the tax year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`ex` `the readings` `the person` `the items` `the tax year` MEANS
    `the exempt amount of the person's qualifying income, reading` `the readings` `:` `the person` `items` `the items` `in the tax year` `the tax year`

GIVEN `the person`   IS AN `An individual`
      `the items`    IS A LIST OF `An item of income`
      `the tax year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`exd` `the person` `the items` `the tax year` MEANS
    `the exempt amount of the person's qualifying income` `the person` `items` `the items` `in the tax year` `the tax year`

GIVEN `the readings` IS A `The readings`
      `the person`   IS AN `An individual`
      `the entity`   IS AN `An entity`
      `the items`    IS A LIST OF `An item of an entity's business income`
      `the tax year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`entx` `the readings` `the person` `the entity` `the items` `the tax year` MEANS
    `the exempt business income of the entity, reading` `the readings` `:` `the person` `entity` `the entity` `items` `the items` `in the tax year` `the tax year`

§§ `Readings I take (named)`

`F2` MEANS `fork F2, the exception for income attributed under section 62A`
`F3` MEANS `fork F3, the ceiling for income received from a relative in 2030`
`F4` MEANS `fork F4, the adaptation year`
`F5` MEANS `fork F5, the unit of the period of residence in 2026`
`F6` MEANS `fork F6, the total cap of section 2(c) in 2026`
`F7` MEANS `fork F7, the residence of the individual in section 3`
`F8` MEANS `fork F8, section 4 and the exemption of an entity`
`F9` MEANS `fork F9, the years in which section 4 counts days in Israel`

`R0` MEANS `the readings this model takes where the text does not decide`

GIVEN `the fork` IS A `A fork`
      `the readings` IS A `The readings`
GIVETH A `The readings`
`first of` `the fork` `on` `the readings` MEANS `the readings with` `the fork` `set to its first reading` TRUE `in` `the readings`

GIVEN `the fork` IS A `A fork`
      `the readings` IS A `The readings`
GIVETH A `The readings`
`second of` `the fork` `on` `the readings` MEANS `the readings with` `the fork` `set to its first reading` FALSE `in` `the readings`

-- AMB-2: paragraph (4) stands in 2030 (F3 first reading).
`T-relative-2030-text` MEANS `first of` `F3` `on` `R0`
-- AMB-1: days, inclusive of the arrival day, over 365 (F5 first reading); the alternative is months (second).
`T-days` MEANS `first of` `F5` `on` `R0`
`T-months` MEANS `second of` `F5` `on` `R0`
-- AMB-6: the adaptation-year election changes nothing (F4 second reading).
`T-adapt-ignored` MEANS `second of` `F4` `on` `R0`
-- F2 reading A: income attributed under s 62A is qualifying although it comes from a transparent corporation (H15).
`T-62A-qualifies` MEANS `first of` `F2` `on` `R0`
-- AMB-7: s 3 exempts only income produced from the day he became resident (F7 first reading).
`T-entity-from-arrival` MEANS `first of` `F7` `on` `R0`
-- AMB-5: s 4 does not touch the entity's exemption (F8 second reading).
`T-s4-spares-entity` MEANS `second of` `F8` `on` `R0`
`T-s4-takes-entity` MEANS `first of` `F8` `on` `R0`
-- AMB-4: the literal reading, either year 2028 or 2029 (F9 first reading); alternative: the year of ceasing (second).
`T-days-either-year` MEANS `first of` `F9` `on` `R0`
`T-days-year-of-ceasing` MEANS `second of` `F9` `on` `R0`

§§ `Persons`

-- A01: first resident on 5 November 2025.
`T-full` MEANS `an immigrant who first became an Israeli resident on` (YMD 2025 11 5)
-- B-cases and D-cases use the same person: resident throughout 2026 to 2030.

-- Pro rata arrivals in 2026 (C-cases): days to 31 December, inclusive of the arrival day.
`T-mar15` MEANS `an immigrant who first became an Israeli resident on` (YMD 2026 3 15)
`T-oct20` MEANS `an immigrant who first became an Israeli resident on` (YMD 2026 10 20)
`T-aug8`  MEANS `an immigrant who first became an Israeli resident on` (YMD 2026 8 8)
`T-may27` MEANS `an immigrant who first became an Israeli resident on` (YMD 2026 5 27)
`T-jul1`  MEANS `an immigrant who first became an Israeli resident on` (YMD 2026 7 1)
`T-dec31` MEANS `an immigrant who first became an Israeli resident on` (YMD 2026 12 31)
`T-jan2`  MEANS `an immigrant who first became an Israeli resident on` (YMD 2026 1 2)
`T-jan1`  MEANS `an immigrant who first became an Israeli resident on` (YMD 2026 1 1)

§§ `A. Who is covered, and the window`

-- A01 A02 A03 A04: both ends of the window, inclusive.
#ASSERT `the person is within section 2(a)` (`an immigrant who first became an Israeli resident on` (YMD 2025 11 5))
#ASSERT NOT `the person is within section 2(a)` (`an immigrant who first became an Israeli resident on` (YMD 2025 11 4))
#ASSERT `the person is within section 2(a)` (`an immigrant who first became an Israeli resident on` (YMD 2026 12 31))
#ASSERT NOT `the person is within section 2(a)` (`an immigrant who first became an Israeli resident on` (YMD 2027 1 1))
-- A02 A04 in amounts: nothing is exempt for someone outside the window.
#ASSERT `exd` (`an immigrant who first became an Israeli resident on` (YMD 2025 11 4)) (LIST (`an employment income of` 100_000 `produced on` (YMD 2027 3 1))) 2027 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `exd` (`an immigrant who first became an Israeli resident on` (YMD 2027 1 1)) (LIST (`an employment income of` 100_000 `produced on` (YMD 2027 3 1))) 2027 EQUALS 0
-- A05: first resident 31 December 2025, 2026 income 700,000: a resident for all of 2026.
#ASSERT `exd` (`an immigrant who first became an Israeli resident on` (YMD 2025 12 31)) (LIST (`an employment income of` 700_000 `produced on` (YMD 2026 6 15))) 2026 EQUALS 600_000
-- A06: first resident 1 January 2026.
#ASSERT `exd` `T-jan1` (LIST (`an employment income of` 700_000 `produced on` (YMD 2026 6 15))) 2026 EQUALS 600_000
-- A07: returning veteran with certificate, 1 March 2026.
#ASSERT `the person is within section 2(a)` (`a veteran returning resident who became an Israeli resident on` (YMD 2026 3 1))
-- A09: veteran without the Ministry's certificate.
#ASSERT NOT `the person is within section 2(a)` (`a returning resident with no certificate, who became an Israeli resident on` (YMD 2026 3 1))
#ASSERT `exd` (`a returning resident with no certificate, who became an Israeli resident on` (YMD 2026 3 1)) (LIST (`an employment income of` 100_000 `produced on` (YMD 2026 9 1))) 2026 EQUALS 0
-- A10: citizenship annulled under s 11 of the Citizenship Law.
#ASSERT NOT `the person is within section 2(a)` (`an oleh whose Israeli citizenship was cancelled under section 11 of the Citizenship Law, who first became an Israeli resident on` (YMD 2026 3 1))
-- A11: a class entitled to an absorption basket, no certificate.
#ASSERT `the person is within section 2(a)` (`an immigrant counted in an absorption basket class, who first became an Israeli resident on` (YMD 2026 3 1))
-- A12: a person who became resident again but not for the first time, and is not a veteran.
#ASSERT NOT `the person is within section 2(a)` (`an immigrant who became an Israeli resident, not for the first time, on` (YMD 2026 3 1))
-- A13: arrival 1 February 2026 with an elected adaptation year: the window test is unaffected (s 2(e)).
#ASSERT `the person is within section 2(a)` (`an immigrant who first became an Israeli resident on` (YMD 2026 2 1) `and elected an adaptation year from` (YMD 2026 2 1))
-- A14 A15: oleh and returning veteran at once: one ceiling.
`T-dual` MEANS `a general individual` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE (YMD 2025 11 5) TRUE NOTHING NOTHING 365 365
#ASSERT `exd` `T-dual` (LIST (`an employment income of` 1_500_000 `produced on` (YMD 2027 3 1))) 2027 EQUALS 1_000_000
#ASSERT `exd` `T-dual` (LIST (`an employment income of` 1_300_000 `produced on` (YMD 2026 3 1))) 2026 EQUALS 600_000

§§ `B. Ceilings by year, full-year resident`

-- B01 to B04: 2026.
#ASSERT `exd` `T-full` (LIST (`an employment income of` 599_999 `produced on` (YMD 2026 6 15))) 2026 EQUALS 599_999
#ASSERT `exd` `T-full` (LIST (`an employment income of` 600_000 `produced on` (YMD 2026 6 15))) 2026 EQUALS 600_000
#ASSERT `exd` `T-full` (LIST (`an employment income of` 600_001 `produced on` (YMD 2026 6 15))) 2026 EQUALS 600_000
#ASSERT `exd` `T-full` (EMPTY) 2026 EQUALS 0
-- B05 to B07: 2027.
#ASSERT `exd` `T-full` (LIST (`an employment income of` 999_999 `produced on` (YMD 2027 6 15))) 2027 EQUALS 999_999
#ASSERT `exd` `T-full` (LIST (`an employment income of` 1_000_000 `produced on` (YMD 2027 6 15))) 2027 EQUALS 1_000_000
#ASSERT `exd` `T-full` (LIST (`an employment income of` 1_000_001 `produced on` (YMD 2027 6 15))) 2027 EQUALS 1_000_000
-- B08 B09: 2028.
#ASSERT `exd` `T-full` (LIST (`an employment income of` 1_500_000 `produced on` (YMD 2028 3 1))) 2028 EQUALS 1_000_000
#ASSERT `exd` `T-full` (LIST (`an employment income of` 1_000_000 `produced on` (YMD 2028 3 1))) 2028 EQUALS 1_000_000
-- B10 to B12: 2029.
#ASSERT `exd` `T-full` (LIST (`an employment income of` 349_999 `produced on` (YMD 2029 3 1))) 2029 EQUALS 349_999
#ASSERT `exd` `T-full` (LIST (`an employment income of` 350_000 `produced on` (YMD 2029 3 1))) 2029 EQUALS 350_000
#ASSERT `exd` `T-full` (LIST (`an employment income of` 350_001 `produced on` (YMD 2029 3 1))) 2029 EQUALS 350_000
-- B13 to B15: 2030.
#ASSERT `exd` `T-full` (LIST (`an employment income of` 149_999 `produced on` (YMD 2030 3 1))) 2030 EQUALS 149_999
#ASSERT `exd` `T-full` (LIST (`an employment income of` 150_000 `produced on` (YMD 2030 3 1))) 2030 EQUALS 150_000
#ASSERT `exd` `T-full` (LIST (`an employment income of` 150_001 `produced on` (YMD 2030 3 1))) 2030 EQUALS 150_000
-- B16 B17: 2031 and 2025.
#ASSERT `exd` `T-full` (LIST (`an employment income of` 100_000 `produced on` (YMD 2031 3 1))) 2031 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `exd` `T-full` (LIST (`an employment income of` 80_000 `produced on` (YMD 2025 12 1))) 2025 EQUALS 0
-- B18: no carry-over from an unused 2027 ceiling.
#ASSERT `exd` `T-full` (LIST (`an employment income of` 500_000 `produced on` (YMD 2029 3 1))) 2029 EQUALS 350_000
-- B19: the remainder is taxable; 2027 with 1,200,000.
#ASSERT `exd` `T-full` (LIST (`an employment income of` 1_200_000 `produced on` (YMD 2027 3 1))) 2027 EQUALS 1_000_000
-- B20: a 2027-sized income in 2026 is capped at the 2026 ceiling.
#ASSERT `exd` `T-full` (LIST (`an employment income of` 1_000_000 `produced on` (YMD 2026 3 1))) 2026 EQUALS 600_000

§§ `C. 2026 pro rata (days, inclusive of the arrival day, over 365); the unit is flagged AMB-1`

-- C01: 15 March, 292 days, 480,000 on days; months (March to December, 10) give 500,000.
#ASSERT `ex` `T-days`   `T-mar15` (LIST (`an employment income of` 1_000_000 `produced on` (YMD 2026 12 31))) 2026 EQUALS 480_000
#ASSERT `ex` `T-months` `T-mar15` (LIST (`an employment income of` 1_000_000 `produced on` (YMD 2026 12 31))) 2026 EQUALS 500_000
#ASSERT REFUSED `exd` `T-mar15` (LIST (`an employment income of` 1_000_000 `produced on` (YMD 2026 12 31))) 2026
-- C02: 20 October, 73 days, 120,000; months (October to December, 3) give 150,000.
#ASSERT `ex` `T-days`   `T-oct20` (LIST (`an employment income of` 1_000_000 `produced on` (YMD 2026 12 31))) 2026 EQUALS 120_000
#ASSERT `ex` `T-months` `T-oct20` (LIST (`an employment income of` 1_000_000 `produced on` (YMD 2026 12 31))) 2026 EQUALS 150_000
#ASSERT REFUSED `exd` `T-oct20` (LIST (`an employment income of` 1_000_000 `produced on` (YMD 2026 12 31))) 2026
-- C03: 8 August, 146 days, 240,000; months give 250,000.
#ASSERT `ex` `T-days`   `T-aug8` (LIST (`an employment income of` 1_000_000 `produced on` (YMD 2026 12 31))) 2026 EQUALS 240_000
#ASSERT `ex` `T-months` `T-aug8` (LIST (`an employment income of` 1_000_000 `produced on` (YMD 2026 12 31))) 2026 EQUALS 250_000
#ASSERT REFUSED `exd` `T-aug8` (LIST (`an employment income of` 1_000_000 `produced on` (YMD 2026 12 31))) 2026
-- C04: 27 May, 219 days, 360,000; months give 400,000.
#ASSERT `ex` `T-days`   `T-may27` (LIST (`an employment income of` 1_000_000 `produced on` (YMD 2026 12 31))) 2026 EQUALS 360_000
#ASSERT `ex` `T-months` `T-may27` (LIST (`an employment income of` 1_000_000 `produced on` (YMD 2026 12 31))) 2026 EQUALS 400_000
#ASSERT REFUSED `exd` `T-may27` (LIST (`an employment income of` 1_000_000 `produced on` (YMD 2026 12 31))) 2026
-- C05: 1 July, 184 days, 110,400,000 / 365 = 302,465.7534; months give 300,000.
#ASSERT `ex` `T-days`   `T-jul1` (LIST (`an employment income of` 1_000_000 `produced on` (YMD 2026 12 31))) 2026 EQUALS 110_400_000 / 365
#ASSERT `ex` `T-months` `T-jul1` (LIST (`an employment income of` 1_000_000 `produced on` (YMD 2026 12 31))) 2026 EQUALS 300_000
#ASSERT REFUSED `exd` `T-jul1` (LIST (`an employment income of` 1_000_000 `produced on` (YMD 2026 12 31))) 2026
-- C06: 31 December, one day, 600,000 / 365 = 1,643.84.
#ASSERT `ex` `T-days` `T-dec31` (LIST (`an employment income of` 1_000_000 `produced on` (YMD 2026 12 31))) 2026 EQUALS 600_000 / 365
#ASSERT REFUSED `exd` `T-dec31` (LIST (`an employment income of` 1_000_000 `produced on` (YMD 2026 12 31))) 2026
-- C07: 2 January, 364 days, 600,000 x 364 / 365.
#ASSERT `ex` `T-days` `T-jan2` (LIST (`an employment income of` 1_000_000 `produced on` (YMD 2026 12 31))) 2026 EQUALS 600_000 * 364 / 365
#ASSERT REFUSED `exd` `T-jan2` (LIST (`an employment income of` 1_000_000 `produced on` (YMD 2026 12 31))) 2026
-- C08: income below both prorated ceilings: the readings agree, the default answers.
#ASSERT `exd` `T-mar15` (LIST (`an employment income of` 400_000 `produced on` (YMD 2026 12 31))) 2026 EQUALS 400_000
-- C09: income of exactly the days ceiling (480,000) is under the months ceiling (500,000): both answer 480,000.
#ASSERT `exd` `T-mar15` (LIST (`an employment income of` 480_000 `produced on` (YMD 2026 12 31))) 2026 EQUALS 480_000
-- C10: 480,001 on days is 480,000, on months 480,001.
#ASSERT `ex` `T-days` `T-mar15` (LIST (`an employment income of` 480_001 `produced on` (YMD 2026 12 31))) 2026 EQUALS 480_000
-- C11: relatives only, 15 March: 140,000 x 292 / 365 = 112,000.
#ASSERT `ex` `T-days` `T-mar15` (LIST (`an employment income received from a relative of` 200_000 `produced on` (YMD 2026 12 31))) 2026 EQUALS 112_000
-- C12: relatives only, 20 October: 140,000 x 73 / 365 = 28,000.
#ASSERT `ex` `T-days` `T-oct20` (LIST (`an employment income received from a relative of` 200_000 `produced on` (YMD 2026 12 31))) 2026 EQUALS 28_000
-- C13: both kinds, 15 March: 100,000 + 112,000.
#ASSERT `ex` `T-days` `T-mar15` (LIST (`an employment income of` 100_000 `produced on` (YMD 2026 12 31)), (`an employment income received from a relative of` 200_000 `produced on` (YMD 2026 12 31))) 2026 EQUALS 212_000
-- C14: 2027 is not prorated for someone who arrived 31 December 2026.
#ASSERT `exd` `T-dec31` (LIST (`an employment income of` 1_000_000 `produced on` (YMD 2027 3 1))) 2027 EQUALS 1_000_000
-- C15: arrival 5 November 2025, 2026 income 700,000: the whole of 2026.
#ASSERT `exd` `T-full` (LIST (`an employment income of` 700_000 `produced on` (YMD 2026 3 1))) 2026 EQUALS 600_000
-- C16: relatives only, 1 July: 140,000 x 184 / 365.
#ASSERT `ex` `T-days` `T-jul1` (LIST (`an employment income received from a relative of` 100_000 `produced on` (YMD 2026 12 31))) 2026 EQUALS 25_760_000 / 365
-- C17: both kinds, 8 August: 100,000 + 140,000 x 146 / 365 = 156,000.
#ASSERT `ex` `T-days` `T-aug8` (LIST (`an employment income of` 100_000 `produced on` (YMD 2026 12 31)), (`an employment income received from a relative of` 100_000 `produced on` (YMD 2026 12 31))) 2026 EQUALS 156_000
-- C18: 27 May, 400,000 against a 360,000 ceiling.
#ASSERT `ex` `T-days` `T-may27` (LIST (`an employment income of` 400_000 `produced on` (YMD 2026 12 31))) 2026 EQUALS 360_000

§§ `D. The relatives' 140,000 (s 2(b), (c))`

-- D01 to D03: 2026, full-year resident.
#ASSERT `exd` `T-full` (LIST (`an employment income received from a relative of` 140_000 `produced on` (YMD 2026 6 15))) 2026 EQUALS 140_000
#ASSERT `exd` `T-full` (LIST (`an employment income received from a relative of` 140_001 `produced on` (YMD 2026 6 15))) 2026 EQUALS 140_000
#ASSERT `exd` `T-full` (LIST (`an employment income received from a relative of` 139_999 `produced on` (YMD 2026 6 15))) 2026 EQUALS 139_999
-- D04 to D06.
#ASSERT `exd` `T-full` (LIST (`an employment income received from a relative of` 500_000 `produced on` (YMD 2027 6 15))) 2027 EQUALS 140_000
#ASSERT `exd` `T-full` (LIST (`an employment income received from a relative of` 140_000 `produced on` (YMD 2028 6 15))) 2028 EQUALS 140_000
#ASSERT `exd` `T-full` (LIST (`an employment income received from a relative of` 200_000 `produced on` (YMD 2029 6 15))) 2029 EQUALS 140_000
-- D07 D08: 2030, paragraph (4) stands; the readings are named (the encoding refuses by default, F3).
#ASSERT `ex` `T-relative-2030-text` `T-full` (LIST (`an employment income received from a relative of` 150_000 `produced on` (YMD 2030 6 15))) 2030 EQUALS 150_000
#ASSERT `ex` `T-relative-2030-text` `T-full` (LIST (`an employment income received from a relative of` 160_000 `produced on` (YMD 2030 6 15))) 2030 EQUALS 150_000
-- D09 D10: both kinds in 2027.
#ASSERT `exd` `T-full` (LIST (`an employment income of` 800_000 `produced on` (YMD 2027 3 1)), (`an employment income received from a relative of` 300_000 `produced on` (YMD 2027 4 1))) 2027 EQUALS 940_000
#ASSERT `exd` `T-full` (LIST (`an employment income of` 950_000 `produced on` (YMD 2027 3 1)), (`an employment income received from a relative of` 300_000 `produced on` (YMD 2027 4 1))) 2027 EQUALS 1_000_000
-- D11: both kinds in 2026, full year.
#ASSERT `exd` `T-full` (LIST (`an employment income of` 500_000 `produced on` (YMD 2026 3 1)), (`an employment income received from a relative of` 200_000 `produced on` (YMD 2026 4 1))) 2026 EQUALS 600_000
-- D12 D13: 2029.
#ASSERT `exd` `T-full` (LIST (`an employment income of` 300_000 `produced on` (YMD 2029 3 1)), (`an employment income received from a relative of` 100_000 `produced on` (YMD 2029 4 1))) 2029 EQUALS 350_000
#ASSERT `exd` `T-full` (LIST (`an employment income received from a relative of` 100_000 `produced on` (YMD 2029 4 1))) 2029 EQUALS 100_000
-- D14: 2030, both kinds, both readings of F3 agree on the total (150,000 against 140,000 + 100,000).
#ASSERT `ex` `T-relative-2030-text` `T-full` (LIST (`an employment income of` 100_000 `produced on` (YMD 2030 3 1)), (`an employment income received from a relative of` 100_000 `produced on` (YMD 2030 4 1))) 2030 EQUALS 150_000
-- D15: income from a company wholly owned by the oleh is not income from a relative.
#ASSERT `exd` `T-full` (LIST (`an employment income received from a company wholly owned by the immigrant, of` 300_000 `produced on` (YMD 2027 3 1))) 2027 EQUALS 300_000
-- D16 D17: received from a relative (the Ordinance fact is an input).
#ASSERT `exd` `T-full` (LIST (`an employment income received from a relative of` 300_000 `produced on` (YMD 2027 3 1))) 2027 EQUALS 140_000
-- D18.
#ASSERT `exd` `T-full` (LIST (`an employment income of` 950_000 `produced on` (YMD 2028 3 1)), (`an employment income received from a relative of` 100_000 `produced on` (YMD 2028 4 1))) 2028 EQUALS 1_000_000

§§ `E. Election "otherwise"`

-- E01: elects that all 800,000 be taxed.
#ASSERT `exd` `T-full` (LIST (`an employment income of` 800_000 `produced on` (YMD 2027 3 1) `of which the individual requested` 800_000 `not to be exempt`)) 2027 EQUALS 0
-- E02: elects on 300,000 of 800,000.
#ASSERT `exd` `T-full` (LIST (`an employment income of` 800_000 `produced on` (YMD 2027 3 1) `of which the individual requested` 300_000 `not to be exempt`)) 2027 EQUALS 500_000
-- E03: 1,200,000, elects on 300,000: 900,000 left, under the ceiling.
#ASSERT `exd` `T-full` (LIST (`an employment income of` 1_200_000 `produced on` (YMD 2027 3 1) `of which the individual requested` 300_000 `not to be exempt`)) 2027 EQUALS 900_000
-- E04: 1,200,000, elects on 100,000: 1,100,000 left, over the ceiling.
#ASSERT `exd` `T-full` (LIST (`an employment income of` 1_200_000 `produced on` (YMD 2027 3 1) `of which the individual requested` 100_000 `not to be exempt`)) 2027 EQUALS 1_000_000
-- E05: election in 2027 does not touch 2028.
#ASSERT `exd` `T-full` (LIST (`an employment income of` 800_000 `produced on` (YMD 2027 3 1) `of which the individual requested` 800_000 `not to be exempt`), (`an employment income of` 500_000 `produced on` (YMD 2028 3 1))) 2028 EQUALS 500_000
-- E06: Q 800,000, R 300,000, elects on all of R.
#ASSERT `exd` `T-full` (LIST (`an employment income of` 800_000 `produced on` (YMD 2027 3 1)), (`a general item of income` (YMD 2027 4 1) 300_000 `work, section 2(2) of the Ordinance` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE 300_000)) 2027 EQUALS 800_000
-- E07: elects on 200,000 of R = 300,000: R left 100,000.
#ASSERT `exd` `T-full` (LIST (`an employment income of` 800_000 `produced on` (YMD 2027 3 1)), (`a general item of income` (YMD 2027 4 1) 300_000 `work, section 2(2) of the Ordinance` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE 200_000)) 2027 EQUALS 900_000
-- E08: the entity asks otherwise.
#ASSERT `entx` `R0` `T-full` (`a non-resident entity that requested otherwise`) (LIST (`an entity's business income through the individual's exertion, of` 500_000 `produced on` (YMD 2027 3 1))) 2027 EQUALS 0
-- E09: 2026 full year, 700,000, elects on 100,000.
#ASSERT `exd` `T-full` (LIST (`an employment income of` 700_000 `produced on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `of which the individual requested` 100_000 `not to be exempt`)) 2026 EQUALS 600_000

§§ `F. Entity income (s 3)`

-- F01: exempt in full, no ceiling.
#ASSERT `entx` `R0` `T-full` (`a plain non-resident entity`) (LIST (`an entity's business income through the individual's exertion, of` 2_000_000 `produced on` (YMD 2027 3 1))) 2027 EQUALS 2_000_000
-- F02: the individual is a material shareholder in the entity.
#ASSERT `entx` `R0` `T-full` (`a non-resident entity in which the individual is a material shareholder`) (LIST (`an entity's business income through the individual's exertion, of` 2_000_000 `produced on` (YMD 2027 3 1))) 2027 EQUALS 0
-- F04 F05 F06 F07: the years.
#ASSERT `entx` `R0` `T-full` (`a plain non-resident entity`) (LIST (`an entity's business income through the individual's exertion, of` 500_000 `produced on` (YMD 2026 3 1))) 2026 EQUALS 500_000
#ASSERT `entx` `R0` `T-full` (`a plain non-resident entity`) (LIST (`an entity's business income through the individual's exertion, of` 500_000 `produced on` (YMD 2030 3 1))) 2030 EQUALS 500_000
#ASSERT `entx` `R0` `T-full` (`a plain non-resident entity`) (LIST (`an entity's business income through the individual's exertion, of` 500_000 `produced on` (YMD 2031 3 1))) 2031 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `entx` `R0` `T-full` (`a plain non-resident entity`) (LIST (`an entity's business income through the individual's exertion, of` 500_000 `produced on` (YMD 2025 12 1))) 2025 EQUALS 0
-- F08: an Israeli-resident entity.
#ASSERT `entx` `R0` `T-full` (`an entity that is not a non-resident entity`) (LIST (`an entity's business income through the individual's exertion, of` 500_000 `produced on` (YMD 2027 3 1))) 2027 EQUALS 0
-- F09: the entity also has Israeli business income that arises without his exertion: the exemption fails.
#ASSERT `entx` `R0` `T-full` (`a plain non-resident entity`) (LIST (`an entity's business income through the individual's exertion, of` 500_000 `produced on` (YMD 2027 3 1)), (`an entity's business income produced in Israel apart from the individual's exertion, of` 100_000 `produced on` (YMD 2027 5 1))) 2027 EQUALS 0
-- F10: a transparent entity (flag taken as true), 250,000 of 1,000,000 attributed to Israeli-resident rights-holders.
#ASSERT `entx` `R0` `T-full` (`a non-resident transparent corporation`) (LIST (`an entity's business income through the individual's exertion, of which` 250_000 `is attributed to Israeli-resident rights-holders, of` 1_000_000 `produced on` (YMD 2027 3 1))) 2027 EQUALS 750_000
-- F11: nothing attributed to an Israeli resident.
#ASSERT `entx` `R0` `T-full` (`a non-resident transparent corporation`) (LIST (`an entity's business income through the individual's exertion, of which` 0 `is attributed to Israeli-resident rights-holders, of` 1_000_000 `produced on` (YMD 2027 3 1))) 2027 EQUALS 1_000_000
-- F12: the entity amount does not use up the person's own ceiling.
#ASSERT `exd` `T-full` (LIST (`an employment income of` 1_000_000 `produced on` (YMD 2027 3 1))) 2027 EQUALS 1_000_000
#ASSERT `entx` `R0` `T-full` (`a plain non-resident entity`) (LIST (`an entity's business income through the individual's exertion, of` 500_000 `produced on` (YMD 2027 3 1))) 2027 EQUALS 500_000
-- F13 (AMB-7): entity income dated before the 2026 arrival (1 July): decided not exempt (F7 first reading); the default is flagged.
#ASSERT `entx` `T-entity-from-arrival` `T-jul1` (`a plain non-resident entity`) (LIST (`an entity's business income through the individual's exertion, of` 500_000 `produced on` (YMD 2026 3 1))) 2026 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT REFUSED `the exempt business income of the entity` `T-jul1` `entity` (`a plain non-resident entity`) `items` (LIST (`an entity's business income through the individual's exertion, of` 500_000 `produced on` (YMD 2026 3 1))) `in the tax year` 2026

§§ `G. Departure (s 4)`

-- Persons: first resident 10 November 2025, ceased on the day, with days in 2028 and 2029.
`T-g01` MEANS `an immigrant who first became an Israeli resident on` (YMD 2025 11 10) `, ceased to be one on` (YMD 2028 6 30) `, and stayed in Israel` 74 `days in 2028 and` 365 `days in 2029`
`T-g02` MEANS `an immigrant who first became an Israeli resident on` (YMD 2025 11 10) `, ceased to be one on` (YMD 2028 6 30) `, and stayed in Israel` 75 `days in 2028 and` 75 `days in 2029`
`T-g03` MEANS `an immigrant who first became an Israeli resident on` (YMD 2025 11 10) `, ceased to be one on` (YMD 2028 6 30) `, and stayed in Israel` 76 `days in 2028 and` 76 `days in 2029`
`T-g04` MEANS `an immigrant who first became an Israeli resident on` (YMD 2025 11 10) `, ceased to be one on` (YMD 2029 3 1) `, and stayed in Israel` 300 `days in 2028 and` 74 `days in 2029`
`T-g05` MEANS `an immigrant who first became an Israeli resident on` (YMD 2025 11 10) `, ceased to be one on` (YMD 2029 3 1) `, and stayed in Israel` 300 `days in 2028 and` 75 `days in 2029`
`T-g06` MEANS `an immigrant who first became an Israeli resident on` (YMD 2025 11 10) `, ceased to be one on` (YMD 2029 3 1) `, and stayed in Israel` 300 `days in 2028 and` 76 `days in 2029`
`T-g07` MEANS `an immigrant who first became an Israeli resident on` (YMD 2025 11 10) `, ceased to be one on` (YMD 2027 10 10) `, and stayed in Israel` 10 `days in 2028 and` 10 `days in 2029`
`T-g08` MEANS `an immigrant who first became an Israeli resident on` (YMD 2025 11 10) `, ceased to be one on` (YMD 2030 4 15) `, and stayed in Israel` 20 `days in 2028 and` 20 `days in 2029`
`T-g09` MEANS `an immigrant who first became an Israeli resident on` (YMD 2025 11 10) `, has not ceased to be one, and stayed in Israel` 20 `days in 2028 and` 20 `days in 2029`
`T-g12` MEANS `an immigrant who first became an Israeli resident on` (YMD 2025 11 10) `, ceased to be one on` (YMD 2028 10 1) `, and stayed in Israel` 275 `days in 2028 and` 30 `days in 2029`
`T-g13` MEANS `an immigrant who first became an Israeli resident on` (YMD 2025 11 10) `, ceased to be one on` (YMD 2028 10 1) `, and stayed in Israel` 275 `days in 2028 and` 0 `days in 2029`
`T-g15` MEANS `an immigrant who first became an Israeli resident on` (YMD 2025 11 10) `, ceased to be one on` (YMD 2029 6 1) `, and stayed in Israel` 365 `days in 2028 and` 365 `days in 2029`

-- G01 G02 G03: 74 switches the Law off, 75 and 76 do not.
#ASSERT `section 4 switches the Law off for the person` `T-g01`
#ASSERT NOT `section 4 switches the Law off for the person` `T-g02`
#ASSERT NOT `section 4 switches the Law off for the person` `T-g03`
-- G04 G05 G06: ceased in 2029.
#ASSERT `section 4 switches the Law off for the person` `T-g04`
#ASSERT NOT `section 4 switches the Law off for the person` `T-g05`
#ASSERT NOT `section 4 switches the Law off for the person` `T-g06`
-- G07 G08: ceased in 2027 or in 2030: not engaged.
#ASSERT NOT `section 4 switches the Law off for the person` `T-g07`
#ASSERT NOT `section 4 switches the Law off for the person` `T-g08`
-- G09: has not ceased.
#ASSERT NOT `section 4 switches the Law off for the person` `T-g09`
-- G10: the 2026 and 2027 exemptions are lost retroactively.
#ASSERT `exd` `T-g01` (LIST (`an employment income of` 600_000 `produced on` (YMD 2026 6 1))) 2026 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `exd` `T-g01` (LIST (`an employment income of` 900_000 `produced on` (YMD 2027 6 1))) 2027 EQUALS 0
-- G11: the 2028 income earned before leaving.
#ASSERT `exd` `T-g01` (LIST (`an employment income of` 400_000 `produced on` (YMD 2028 3 1))) 2028 EQUALS 0
-- G02 G03 in amounts: the Law still applies.
#ASSERT `exd` `T-g02` (LIST (`an employment income of` 500_000 `produced on` (YMD 2026 6 1))) 2026 EQUALS 500_000
#ASSERT `exd` `T-g03` (LIST (`an employment income of` 500_000 `produced on` (YMD 2026 6 1))) 2026 EQUALS 500_000
-- G04 G05 in amounts.
#ASSERT `exd` `T-g04` (LIST (`an employment income of` 500_000 `produced on` (YMD 2026 6 1))) 2026 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `exd` `T-g05` (LIST (`an employment income of` 400_000 `produced on` (YMD 2026 6 1))) 2026 EQUALS 400_000
-- G07: 2027 income earned while resident stands.
#ASSERT `exd` `T-g07` (LIST (`an employment income of` 400_000 `produced on` (YMD 2027 6 1))) 2027 EQUALS 400_000
-- G08: 2030 income before ceasing stands.
#ASSERT `exd` `T-g08` (LIST (`an employment income of` 100_000 `produced on` (YMD 2030 2 1))) 2030 EQUALS 100_000
-- G12 G13 (AMB-4): literal reading disqualifies, the year-of-ceasing reading does not; the default is flagged.
#ASSERT `section 4 switches the Law off for the person, reading` `T-days-either-year` `:` `T-g12`
#ASSERT NOT `section 4 switches the Law off for the person, reading` `T-days-year-of-ceasing` `:` `T-g12`
